verbs.etymology_text:
Of uncertain origin. There are several possibilities for the origin:
* From Latin Latin eruncāre. Compare Romanian arunca and Sicilian arruncari. Possibly influenced by erādīcāre;
* Coromines links it with Old Spanish desrancar (“to evict, to throw out”), compare Galician derrancarse, with an ultimate origin in either Old Occitan renc or Old French ranc (“row”).
